option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION=Ambient Occlusion
option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION.comment=Corners and crevices are a little darker.
option.SUN_RAYS=Sun Rays
option.SUN_RAYS.comment=Sunlight in the air, broken up by trees and openings. Needs Shadows. Only what stands within Shadow Distance breaks it up.
option.SUN_RAYS_STRENGTH=Sun Ray Strength
option.SUN_RAYS_STRENGTH.comment=Soft is only the sunlight in the air. Strong and Insane add thicker air, and shafts fanning out around the sun past hills, trees and far-off terrain, whatever Shadow Distance is.
value.SUN_RAYS_STRENGTH.1=Soft
value.SUN_RAYS_STRENGTH.2=Strong
value.SUN_RAYS_STRENGTH.3=Insane
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Water reflects the land around it, not just the sky.
option.WAVING=Waving
option.WAVING.comment=Water ripples; leaves and plants sway.
option.PBR=Resource Pack PBR
option.PBR.comment=Bumpy surfaces, shine, metal and glowing ores from a LabPBR resource pack's normal and specular maps, such as Vanilla Mashup PBR. Does nothing without such a pack. Entities and held items are not affected.
option.POM=Parallax Depth
option.POM.comment=Makes surfaces look deep, using the resource pack's height maps, so cobblestone and bricks stand out instead of just looking bumpy. Costs speed, most with High quality. Needs Resource Pack PBR. Not on plants, leaves or glass.
option.POM_DEPTH=Depth
option.POM_DEPTH.comment=How deep surfaces look, up to a quarter of a block at 100%.
